WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.190
Picture one page of a novel.

2
00:00:02.190 --> 00:00:04.790
A kitchen. A mother sewing.

3
00:00:04.790 --> 00:00:06.820
Her son leaves for Paris:

4
00:00:06.820 --> 00:00:08.990
«Le car est à six heures.» She puts his

5
00:00:08.990 --> 00:00:12.330
shirt on the table, a button sewn back on.

6
00:00:12.330 --> 00:00:16.420
He says: «Merci, maman.» She
gets up to heat the soup.

7
00:00:16.420 --> 00:00:18.680
You get 20 minutes with that page.

8
00:00:18.680 --> 00:00:20.860
Then 3 to 4 minutes of talk,

9
00:00:20.860 --> 00:00:25.180
in French. So what do you
actually say about one page,

10
00:00:25.180 --> 00:00:27.320
out loud? In this mission,

11
00:00:27.320 --> 00:00:29.910
you'll map the oral: two extracts,

12
00:00:29.910 --> 00:00:32.170
one choice, three parts.

13
00:00:32.170 --> 00:00:34.950
Then you'll plan your 20
minutes on a prep clock,

14
00:00:34.950 --> 00:00:36.990
five tasks in a row.

15
00:00:36.990 --> 00:00:40.830
Your mission: work out what
to say about a single page,

16
00:00:40.830 --> 00:00:42.610
in French, out loud.
